WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.420
The Department of Justice has uncovered
a sprawling college admissions scandal.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:14.100
While condemnation has justifiably rained
down on the rich parents who paid bribes,

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.320
the colleges in question are equally
culpable. College staff were complicit

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:22.410
in these schemes or asleep at
the switch. These same colleges won't

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:26.699
abolish legacy admissions or stop
reserving seats for the kids of big

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:31.560
donors. If admissions offices can't
detect corruption and colleges can't

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:36.989
stop selling access, maybe colleges can't
be trusted to judge merit fairly.

00:00:36.989 --> 00:00:41.610
So, here's a modest proposal: Elite colleges
can put their money where their mouth is

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:45.809
when they talk about democratizing
opportunity, take a page out of the K-12

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:50.879
charter school playbook, and switch to
lottery admissions. Any applicant with a

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:55.140
high school credential would have an
equal shot at admission. Admittedly, this

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:59.579
would be a huge blow to the prestige of
elite colleges, a pain for corporate

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:04.320
HR departments, and a giant bummer
for the college prep industry.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.700
But I think we'd survive. How do you think
we should reform college admissions?

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:14.320
Let us know in the comments. Also, let us 
know what other topics you'd like our scholars

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:21.040
to cover in 60 seconds and be sure to LIKE and
subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

